Clearing browsing history from Clear browsing data, and dismissing the dialog, tell the
BrowserView's element, which Chrome CHECKs is there. A window of the core's has no BrowserView, so
Delete with history ticked crashed the browser (#1821), and on Chromium 157 so would Cancel, which
tells the element too. 157 does both through NotifyBrowserViewCustomEvent(), so the event is skipped
there when there's no element. Chromium 156's version is chromium-core-clear-history-element.patch.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,12 @@
   ui::TrackedElement* const browser_element =
       ui::ElementTracker::GetElementTracker()->GetUniqueElement(
           kBrowserViewElementId, context);
-  CHECK(browser_element);
+  // browser_core: a window of the core's has no BrowserView, so there's no
+  // element to tell, and the history is cleared, or the dialog dismissed, all
+  // the same.
+  if (!browser_element) {
+    return;
+  }
   ui::ElementTracker::GetFrameworkDelegate()->NotifyCustomEvent(browser_element,
                                                                 event_type);
 }
